IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il44-nouns`
IMPORT `il44-references`

-- Row il-44. The sound references of section 12A1(a) and the days, as assertions that hold. The one reference that does not hold is in `il44-tests-expected-red.l4`.

§ `The controls point at what they say`

#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` `reference C1: 12A1(a)(1) to section 32 of the Ordinance`
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` `reference C2: 12A1(a)(2)(a) to section 34 of the Ordinance`
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` `reference C3: 12A1(a)(2)(b) to section 39 of the Ordinance`
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` `reference C4: 12A1(a)(1) to section 128 of the Law`
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` `reference C5: 12A1(a)(1) to section 130 of the Law`
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` `reference C6: 12(b)(2) to section 32 of the Ordinance`

§ `The controls name one instrument for one section number`

-- Paragraph (1) of section 12A1(a) and section 12(b)(2) both name the Ordinance for section 32.
#ASSERT `the two citations name the same instrument for the same section number` `reference C1: 12A1(a)(1) to section 32 of the Ordinance` `reference C6: 12(b)(2) to section 32 of the Ordinance`
-- Different section numbers: the test is vacuous and holds.
#ASSERT `the two citations name the same instrument for the same section number` `reference C2: 12A1(a)(2)(a) to section 34 of the Ordinance` `reference C3: 12A1(a)(2)(b) to section 39 of the Ordinance`
#ASSERT `the two citations name the same instrument for the same section number` `reference C4: 12A1(a)(1) to section 128 of the Law` `reference C5: 12A1(a)(1) to section 130 of the Law`

§ `Where each side of a citation was read`

-- The citing words of every row below were read from the page image of the instrument that wrote them (SH 1808 p. 568, or SH 3441 p. 725 for C6).
#ASSERT `reference D1: 12A1(a)(2)(b) to section 32, as written`'s `the citing words were read` EQUALS `read from the page image of the official instrument`
#ASSERT `reference C1: 12A1(a)(1) to section 32 of the Ordinance`'s `the citing words were read` EQUALS `read from the page image of the official instrument`
#ASSERT `reference C6: 12(b)(2) to section 32 of the Ordinance`'s `the citing words were read` EQUALS `read from the page image of the official instrument`
-- The target of D1 was read from the page image of the instrument that repealed it (SH 1592 p. 350). The targets of the controls were read in the consolidations only.
#ASSERT `reference D1: 12A1(a)(2)(b) to section 32, as written`'s `the target was read` EQUALS `read from the page image of the official instrument`
#ASSERT `reference C1: 12A1(a)(1) to section 32 of the Ordinance`'s `the target was read` EQUALS `read in the Wikisource consolidation only`
#ASSERT `reference C2: 12A1(a)(2)(a) to section 34 of the Ordinance`'s `the target was read` EQUALS `read in the Wikisource consolidation only`
#ASSERT `reference C3: 12A1(a)(2)(b) to section 39 of the Ordinance`'s `the target was read` EQUALS `read in the Wikisource consolidation only`
#ASSERT `reference C4: 12A1(a)(1) to section 128 of the Law`'s `the target was read` EQUALS `read in the Wikisource consolidation only`
#ASSERT `reference C5: 12A1(a)(1) to section 130 of the Law`'s `the target was read` EQUALS `read in the Wikisource consolidation only`
#ASSERT `reference C6: 12(b)(2) to section 32 of the Ordinance`'s `the target was read` EQUALS `read in the Wikisource consolidation only`

§ `The days`

-- The repeal was published before the words of 2001 were; on either reading of "at the end of one year from its publication" it had taken effect before them, and about four years before.
#ASSERT `the day Sefer HaChukim 1592 was published` LESS THAN `the earliest first day of force of the repeal`
#ASSERT `the earliest first day of force of the repeal` AT MOST `the latest first day of force of the repeal`
#ASSERT `the latest first day of force of the repeal` LESS THAN `the day Sefer HaChukim 1808 was published`
#ASSERT `the day Sefer HaChukim 1808 was published` LESS THAN `the day Sefer HaChukim 3441 was published`
